{
  "slug": "artist:bigbang",
  "name": "BIGBANG",
  "editorial_article": "Formed by YG Entertainment in 2006, the South Korean boy band BIGBANG became a leading force in the Korean Wave through their blend of hip hop, R&B, and electronic production. Their breakout single, the 2007 track 'Lies' composed by leader G-Dragon, dominated South Korean charts for a record-breaking six consecutive weeks and secured the group a foothold as pioneers of the K-pop genre. Throughout their career, the members maintained significant creative control, writing and producing their own material, which expanded from early hip-hop roots to include diverse influences such as rock and experimental dance. Following a period of hiatus and lineup transitions, the group reunited for a surprise performance at the 2024 MAMA Awards in Osaka. In 2026, the trio announced their 20th-anniversary XX: COSMOS world tour, marking two decades since their debut at Seoul's Olympic Gymnastics Arena.",
